    {
      "title": "NDIS data may have ended up in Palantir’s analytics platform as part of efforts to curb fraud",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/09/ndis-data-may-have-ended-up-in-palantirs-analytics-platform-as-part-of-efforts-to-curb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> The Australian Criminal Intelligence Commission, which has access to NDIA data, used Palantir as part of a multi-agency fraud taskforce  </p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Personal information of national disability insurance scheme participants may have ended up in controversial software company Palantir’s analytics platform as part of a massive multi-agency sharing program investigating fraud, Guardian Australia can reveal.</p><p>There have been calls to ban the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/apr/30/palantir-manifesto-australia-government-contracts\">use of Palantir’s software by the Australian government since May</a>, after it implied some cultures are inferior to others in a manifesto described by one UK MP as the “ramblings of a supervillain”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/09/ndis-data-may-have-ended-up-in-palantirs-analytics-platform-as-part-of-efforts-to-curb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T01:09:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australia considers new Israel sanctions but won’t join UK in banning trade with ‘settler terrorists’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/09/australia-considers-new-israel-sanctions-but-wont-join-uk-in-banning-trade-with-settler-terrorists-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Penny Wong has concerns about blanket ban announced by UK, France and Canada, but says new ‘targeted measures’ planned over Israeli settlers</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/09/coalition-victoria-energy-bills-labor-one-nation-super-digital-duty-of-care-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia is preparing another round of sanctions against Israel, but has stopped short of joining the UK in banning trade with Israeli settlements in the West Bank.</p><p>Overnight, the UK government offered its <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">strongest condemnation yet of Israel’s occupation</a>, with the foreign secretary, Ed Miliband, calling efforts to control the West Bank unlawful. He said his government agreed there was “ethnic cleansing of Palestinians in areas of the West Bank, perpetrated by settler terrorists.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/09/australia-considers-new-israel-sanctions-but-wont-join-uk-in-banning-trade-with-settler-terrorists-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T01:38:02"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel to close British consulate in Jerusalem after sanctions announced",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/israel-close-british-consulate-jerusalem-sanctions",
      "description": "<p>Several MPs also banned from Israel after UK steps up condemnation of settlements and announces sweeping sanctions</p><p>Israel has ordered the closure of the British consulate in occupied East Jerusalem in response to sweeping UK sanctions on goods from illegal settlements.</p><p>Reacting to Ed Miliband’s description of violent Jewish settler activity on the occupied Palestinian West Bank as <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">“ethnic cleansing” carried out with the tacit backing of the Netanyahu government</a>, Israel’s foreign minister, Gideon Sa’ar, announced retaliatory measures including the closure of the consulate and entry bans on several UK MPs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/israel-close-british-consulate-jerusalem-sanctions\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-08T16:55:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Ed Miliband has overturned decades of Foreign Office inertia on illegal Israeli settlements",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/ed-miliband-overturned-decades-foreign-office-inertia-illegal-israeli-settlements",
      "description": "<p>Foreign secretary ends UK’s feigned helplessness with sanctions and condemnation of ‘ethnic cleansing’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/israel-close-british-consulate-jerusalem-sanctions\">Will UK sanctions have any impact on ‘settler terrorists’? </a></p></li></ul><p>The indefatigable ability of UK Foreign Office ministers over decades to issue boilerplate statements of concern about the extension of illegal settlements in Israel has long been a matter of ridicule.</p><p>Even some of the Conservative ministers who issued them, notably Alan Duncan and Alistair Burt, have agreed. Duncan described the UK stance towards settlements as weak and naive, while Burt wondered at the ability of the Foreign Office to find new forms of diplomatic condemnation that never amounted to any specific action. Margaret Thatcher, often torn as prime minister between her natural sympathy for Israel and her fear of the Gulf states falling under the sway of the Soviet Union, similarly expressed her anger at the settlements.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/ed-miliband-overturned-decades-foreign-office-inertia-illegal-israeli-settlements\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-08T18:34:03"
    },
